{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"OESA-2026-4954","published":"2026-11-19T01:43:26Z","modified":"2026-11-19T02:00:17.940891654Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-129483"],"summary":"cyrus-sasl security update","details":"The  package contains the Cyrus implementation of SASL. SASL is the Simple Authentication and Security Layer, a method for adding authentication support to connection-based protocols.\r\n\r\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\nCyrus SASL through 2.1.28 contains an authentication bypass vulnerability in the SRP server mechanism because srp_server_mech_step2 does not reject client public values A that are multiples of N. Unauthenticated network clients can send A equal to N to force a zero shared secret, authenticating as any existing user without the password and learning session keys.(CVE-2026-129483)","affected":[{"package":{"name":"cyrus-sasl","ecosystem":"openEuler:22.03-LTS-SP4","purl":"pkg:rpm/openEuler/cyrus-sasl&distro=openEuler-22.03-LTS-SP4"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"2.1.28-9.oe2203sp4"}]}],"ecosystem_specific":{"aarch64":["cyrus-sasl-2.1.28-9.oe2203sp4.aarch64.rpm","cyrus-sasl-debuginfo-2.1.28-9.oe2203sp4.aarch64.rpm","cyrus-sasl-debugsource-2.1.28-9.oe2203sp4.aarch64.rpm","cyrus-sasl-devel-2.1.28-9.oe2203sp4.aarch64.rpm","cyrus-sasl-lib-2.1.28-9.oe2203sp4.aarch64.rpm","cyrus-sasl-sql-2.1.28-9.oe2203sp4.aarch64.rpm"],"noarch":["cyrus-sasl-help-2.1.28-9.oe2203sp4.noarch.rpm"],"src":["cyrus-sasl-2.1.28-9.oe2203sp4.src.rpm"],"x86_64":["cyrus-sasl-2.1.28-9.oe2203sp4.x86_64.rpm","cyrus-sasl-debuginfo-2.1.28-9.oe2203sp4.x86_64.rpm","cyrus-sasl-debugsource-2.1.28-9.oe2203sp4.x86_64.rpm","cyrus-sasl-devel-2.1.28-9.oe2203sp4.x86_64.rpm","cyrus-sasl-lib-2.1.28-9.oe2203sp4.x86_64.rpm","cyrus-sasl-sql-2.1.28-9.oe2203sp4.x86_64.rpm"]},"database_specific":{"source":"https://repo.openeuler.org/security/data/osv/OESA-2026-4954.json"}}],"references":[{"type":"ADVISORY","url":"https://www.openeuler.org/zh/security/security-bulletins/detail/?